 "final_message": "I implemented `price_cart` in `cart/pricing.py` following the README rules. All 7 tests pass.\n\nHow it works:\n- **Bulk discount:** each line with `qty >= 10` gets 10% off its amount, rounded half-up with integer math `(amount * 10 + 50) // 100`.\n- **Coupon:** applied to the post-bulk remainder. `PERCENT:<n>` uses the same half-up rounding, and `FIXED:<cents>` is capped at the remainder so the total never goes below zero.\n- **Validation:** raises `ValueError` for quantity below 1, negative unit price, malformed coupons (the prefix must be upper case and the number digits only), and percentages outside 1..100.\n\nI haven't added tests beyond the existing suite for the validation paths.",
